---
layout: base.njk
title: Costs
wide: true
description: "Open operating-cost ledger: billed, AI usage and noncash attention, kept separate. Unknown means unknown."
---
<p class="kicker">Open books · manual ledger</p>
<h1>What this costs</h1>
<p class="lede">If we can explain how to run it, we should explain what it costs.</p>
<div class="notice">
  <p>Billing integrations: <span class="badge pending">{{ costs.billing_integrations }}</span>. Every entry is entered by hand from <a href="{% sourceLink "launch/costs.json" %}"><code>launch/costs.json</code></a>, as of {{ costs.as_of_utc }}. {{ costs.note }}</p>
</div>

{% macro amount(v) %}{% if v === null %}<span class="badge unknown">unknown</span>{% else %}${{ v }}{% endif %}{% endmacro %}

<h2>Billed expenses</h2>
<div class="table-scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">Provider</th><th scope="col">Amount ({{ costs.currency }})</th><th scope="col">Status</th><th scope="col">Source</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {%- for e in costs.billed %}
    <tr><td>{{ e.item }}</td><td>{{ e.provider }}</td><td class="num">{{ amount(e.amount) }}</td><td><span class="badge {{ e.status }}">{{ e.status }}</span></td><td>{{ e.source }}</td></tr>
  {%- endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>

<h2>AI usage</h2>
<div class="table-scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">Provider</th><th scope="col">Amount ({{ costs.currency }})</th><th scope="col">Status</th><th scope="col">Source</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {%- for e in costs.ai_usage %}
    <tr><td>{{ e.item }}</td><td>{{ e.provider }}</td><td class="num">{{ amount(e.amount) }}</td><td><span class="badge {{ e.status }}">{{ e.status }}</span></td><td>{{ e.source }}</td></tr>
  {%- endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>

<h2>Human attention (noncash)</h2>
<p>This is reported separately and never added to billed totals. No method or hourly rate has been adopted. <a href="/charter/#human-attention">Human Attention Accounting</a> is an open proposal.</p>
<div class="table-scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">Hours</th><th scope="col">Valuation</th><th scope="col">Status</th><th scope="col">Source</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {%- for e in costs.noncash_attention %}
    <tr><td>{{ e.item }}</td><td class="num">{{ amount(e.hours) if e.hours === null else e.hours }}</td><td class="num">{{ amount(e.valuation) }}</td><td><span class="badge {{ e.status }}">{{ e.status }}</span></td><td>{{ e.source }}</td></tr>
  {%- endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>

<h2>Propose a saving</h2>
<p>Know a cheaper or sturdier way to run this? Open a pull request with before-and-after unit costs, your estimate method and the risks. See <a href="{% sourceLink "AGENTS.md" %}"><code>AGENTS.md</code></a>.</p>
